  "column_meaning": "The column is the ORDINAL of a value on the located row (extract.py :604-606, 'column': i), not a name. Which thing it stands for depends on the section: in entity sections (S01, S03, S18 in the census: no axes) c0 is the first compared security and c1 the second; in S14/S15/S16 the first label hit is one entity row and the columns are its periods (census axes window/lookback: 5 entries). Nothing on the wire says which: a section carries the eight keys only; the answer's data holds request_ref ids, vendor_artifact, effective_inputs (read_back, holdings_fingerprint, an open settings map), extraction_validation, extraction_coverage; no entity name or period label (contracts/wire/AnalysisReport.ts :12-100; schema section_id is a plain string).",
